>
>## Transform a let-term by pulling all polymorphic let bindings to the top level. This is useful to ensure that polymorphic bindings are not nested within other terms, which is unsupported by certain targets such as Java. Polymorphic bindings are those with a non-empty list of type scheme variables. If a hoisted binding captures lambda-bound variables from an enclosing scope, the binding is wrapped in lambdas for those variables, and references are replaced with applications. Note: Assumes no variable shadowing; use hydra.core.rewriting.unshadowVariables first.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
